"text": "Worked for 45s\n\n### PR #1 review — `sparesparrow/zigbeendicate-sounds`\n\nOverall assessment: Good architectural direction, but I would not merge this PR yet.\n\nThe three interfaces are reasonably separated, and reusing `ZigbeeLightController` is the right architectural decision. However, the implementation introduces several problems involving shared state, blocking I/O, unauthenticated control surfaces, and lifecycle management.\n\nThe most important distinction: this application is not merely exposing information. Its REST and MCP interfaces can physically control devices on the local network. They should be treated as privileged control interfaces.\n\n### 1\\. Critical findings\n\n| Severity | File / lines                                        | Finding                                                               |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|          | api_server.py:119-124, 128-136                      | No authentication; wildcard CORS                                      |\n|          | api_server.py:159-164, mcp_zigbee_server.py:104-106 | MCP does not validate light names                                     |\n|          | mcp_zigbee_server.py:294-299                        | SSE transport lacks an explicit authentication/security configuration |\n|          | api_server.py:66-73, 101-105                        | Controller initialization race and ignored connection ",
